<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovakia posts Q1-Q3 c/a deficit of $1.032 bln.</title>
<headline>Slovakia posts Q1-Q3 c/a deficit of $1.032 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Slovak current account recorded a deficit for the January-September period of $1.032 billion, compared with a $588.1 million surplus over the same period in 1995, the National Bank of Slovakia said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It added that the capital account was in surplus for the first nine months of 1996 by $1.203 billion, compared with a surplus of $222.5 million in the same period the previous year.  </p>
<p>  SLOVAK CURRENT ACCT   9MO'96   8MO'96   9MO'95   FY/95</p>
<p>  overall ($ million) -1,031.7   -957.3  +588.1   +648.8</p>
<p>  trade balance	 -1,221.6 -1,160.4   -13.0    +24.1</p>
<p>  balance of services    +79.0   +103.7  +535.5   +546.2</p>
<p>  income balance	   -23.2    +18.5    +5.1    -13.7</p>
<p>  current transfers     +134.1    +80.8   +60.5    +92.2</p>
<p>CAPITAL ACCOUNT</p>
<p> Total balance	     +1,202.9 +1,111.5  +222.5  +993.9</p>
<p> capital transfers	    +29.9    +29.9   +45.6   +45.7</p>
<p>direct investment balance</p>
<p>  inv. in Slovak republic  +116.8    +68.9  +145.8  +141.9</p>
<p>  Slovak investment abroad  -18.2     -8.4    -5.8    -7.9</p>
<p>portfolio investment balance</p>
<p>  inv. in Slovak Republic    +6.7    +12.1    +7.2   +74.4</p>
<p>  Slovak investment abroad  +38.4    +85.3   +91.0  +171.7</p>
<p>other long-term financial</p>
<p>  account			+385.5   +417.8   +70.8  +393.8</p>
<p> short-term fin. account   +643.7   +505.9   -57.2   +91.3</p>
<p>Note. All figures are in millions of U.S. dollars. The central bank used the following exchange rates in calculating the figures: Jan-Sept '96 (USD=30.427 SKK), Jan-Aug'96 (USD=30.427 SKK), full year '95 (USD=29.735 SKK), Jan-Sept '95 (USD=29.799).</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-536-3687</p>
